TEXT -128 224 Left 2 ;AT samephased operation: (all phases have 0 degrees therefore no 1,a,a^2 used which is for 120degrees difference)\nX1a=(XL11-0.5*XM12-0.5*XM13)=3.4425\nX1b=(XL22-0.5*XM21-0.5*XM23)=3.16\nX1c=(XL33-0.5*XM32-0.5*XM31)=3.4425\nMean value = about 3.34 (for Z1,Z2 see ATP-matrix for symm. components index 2.1, index 0.0 = Z0)
TEXT 144 24 Left 2 ;The resistance from the ATP-Matrix\nis not used as coupled element. The resistance with 0.1626ohm \nis added without coupling. \nMaybe this is not really OK but the difference is \nsmall see below\n \nHINT: If you simulate a nonsymmetric case (Earth fault,..) the coupled\nmodel MUST be used because the uncoupled produces a much \nto high short circuit current value
